      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2019-june/q1",
      "question": "<p>[<em>In this question position vectors are given relative to a fixed origin</em> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>]</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geqslant 0\"></span>, a particle, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, moves so that its velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf v\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf v=6t\\mathbf i-5t^{\\frac32}\\mathbf j\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span>, the position vector of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-20\\mathbf i+20\\mathbf j)\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Find the position vector of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
