      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2019-june/q5",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:90mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2019-june/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3: points A and B 50 m apart on horizontal ground; ball P projected from A at 20 m/s at 30 degrees above AB towards B; ball Q projected from B at u m/s at angle theta above BA towards A.\"></figure><p>The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> lie <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"50\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> apart on horizontal ground.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span> two small balls, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>, are projected in the vertical plane containing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>.</p><p>Ball <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is projected from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>.</p><p>Ball <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> is projected from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> at angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BA\"></span>, as shown in Figure 3.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\"></span> seconds, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> collide.</p><p>Until they collide, the balls are modelled as particles moving freely under gravity.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the velocity of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> at the instant before it collides with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Find<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the size of angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span>,</li><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol></li><li>State one limitation of the model, other than air resistance, that could affect the accuracy of your answers. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
